From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yan <Yan>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:44:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - region tick-thread count: all processors,
 measured

Upstream resolved threads: -1 to totalCores/2 then /4 (<=4 -> 1), which
serialises every region onto ONE tick thread on any host with <= 8 cores
(and only 2 threads on 16 cores).

This matched Folia's own default of half the processors until it was
measured. On an 8-core host under identical block-tick load, one restart
between arms, 8 threads against that default of 4 cut mean MSPT 32%
(25.07 -> 17.17ms) and the tail 62% (48.7 -> 18.3ms) while using LESS
average CPU: the 4-thread arm spent its time contending. A 48.7ms maximum
against a 50ms budget is a tick nearly missed.

A region only ever ticks on one thread, so this is a ceiling on
parallelism rather than a reservation -- threads past the number of
disconnected active regions simply idle. Operators who need cores held
back for chunk workers or Netty set threads: N explicitly, which this
does not touch.

availableProcessors() (not OSNuma total cores) so container CPU quotas
are respected. See docs/architecture/region-parallelism.md.

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/TickRegions.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/TickRegions.java
index abcc8ae0a5ab4d089c6e888519b1b094a9ddcc4d..bf3ea5c66a178a914787bb9bc6697cf9c3ad4c2c 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/TickRegions.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/TickRegions.java
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 package io.papermc.paper.threadedregions;
 
 import ca.spottedleaf.common.util.TimeUtil;
-import ca.spottedleaf.concurrentutil.numa.OSNuma;
 import ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.common.util.TickThread;
 import ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system.scheduling.ChunkHolderManager;
 import com.mojang.logging.LogUtils;
@@ -59,12 +58,25 @@ public final class TickRegions implements ThreadedRegionizer.RegionCallbacks<Tic
     private static int getTickThreads(final GlobalConfiguration.@NonNull ThreadedRegions config) {
         int tickThreads;
         if (config.threads <= 0) {
-            tickThreads = OSNuma.getNativeInstance().getTotalCores() / 2;
-            if (tickThreads <= 4) {
-                tickThreads = 1;
-            } else {
-                tickThreads =  tickThreads / 4;
-            }
+            // SourbyCraft - sane default region tick-thread count
+            // Upstream resolved -1 to totalCores/2 then /4 (<=4 -> 1), which gives ONE region tick
+            // thread on any host with <= 8 cores and only 2 on 16 cores — the whole region-threaded
+            // engine ends up serialised onto a single thread while the remaining cores idle.
+            //
+            // Folia's own default is half the processors, and this matched it until it was
+            // measured. On an 8-core host under identical block-tick load, 8 threads against that
+            // default of 4 cut mean MSPT 32% (25.07 -> 17.17ms) and the tail 62% (48.7 -> 18.3ms),
+            // while using LESS average CPU — the 4-thread arm spent its time contending. A 48.7ms
+            // maximum against a 50ms budget is a tick nearly missed, so half is not a safe default;
+            // it is a quieter way to run out of headroom. See docs/architecture/region-parallelism.md.
+            //
+            // A region only ever ticks on one thread, so this is a ceiling on parallelism, not a
+            // reservation: threads past the number of disconnected active regions simply idle,
+            // which is why raising it costs nothing on a world that cannot use them. An operator
+            // who needs cores held back for chunk workers or Netty sets threads: N explicitly.
+            //
+            // availableProcessors() (not OSNuma total cores) so container CPU quotas are respected.
+            tickThreads = Math.max(1, Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors());
         } else {
             tickThreads = config.threads;
         }
